\section{System Architecture}
The Blocks o' Code v3 architecture relies on a distributed network of child blocks communicating over an I\textsuperscript{2}C bus to a central Brain block. The Brain block continuously polls the bus, validates the current block configuration, and transmits the state via Wi-Fi to a dedicated TCP server. The server interfaces with a Flutter application, allowing users to validate and execute their physical code. 

